"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"├── CAD Product Structure"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Multi-Level BOM System"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Engineering Change Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"├── PDM Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"├── PLM Data Model"},{"type":"p","text":"├── CAD Metadata Automation"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Product Data Quality Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"├── ERP / PLM Integration Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Digital Thread Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"The portfolio should demonstrate that the student understands both engineering information and enterprise data management."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. → Digital Manufacturing & Design → Product Data Manager is best positioned as a hybrid engineering + PLM + product-data career."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["CAD","Engineering Data","PDM/PLM","BOM","Configuration Management","Change Management","SQL/Python","ERP","Digital Manufacturing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For long-term growth, the strongest directions are PLM Consulting, Product Data Architecture, Configuration Management, Digital Thread, Digital Manufacturing and Enterprise PLM Architecture."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Product Data Analyst","Product Data Manager","Senior PLM/Product Data Specialist","PLM Solution Architect","Digital Product Lifecycle / Digital Manufacturing Leader"]}]}]}